es us endless opportunities to be part of the give-and-take of networking. Some worry that this new environment makes us isolated and lonely. But in Networked, Lee Rainie and Barry Wellman show how the large, loosely knit social circles of networked individuals expand opportunities for learning, problem solving, decision making, and personal interaction. The new social operating system of “networked individualism” liberates us from the restrictions of tightly knit groups; it also requires us to develop networking skills and strategies, work on maintaining ties, and balance multiple overlapping networks. Rainie and Wellman outline the “triple revolution” that has brought on this transformation: the rise of social networking, the capacity of the Internet to empower individuals, and the always-on connectivity of mobile devices.","publicationYear":2012,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Social aspects","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-networked-the-new-social-operating-system-lee-rainie-and-barry-wellman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Interpersonal relations","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-networked-the-new-social-operating-system-lee-rainie-and-barry-wellman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Online social networks","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-networked-the-new-social-operating-system-lee-rainie-and-barry-wellman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Social networks","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-networked-the-new-social-operating-system-lee-rainie-and-barry-wellman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Internet","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-networked-the-new-social-operating-system-lee-rainie-and-barry-wellman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Web","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-networked-the-new-so